This project is an original implementation. It is not a fork of, and does not
redistribute code from, any of the projects listed below. They are recorded
because they are dependencies, prior art, or sources of the threat taxonomy
this project measures against, and because that debt should be visible.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
DEPENDENCY

Model Context Protocol Python SDK ("mcp")
  https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/python-sdk
  Copyright (c) Anthropic, PBC and contributors
  Licensed under the MIT License.

  Used as the protocol implementation: the gateway speaks MCP through this SDK
  rather than reimplementing the wire format. Installed as a normal dependency;
  no SDK source is vendored into this repository.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
PRIOR ART, NOT USED AS CODE

The attack taxonomy in corpus/ was derived from public descriptions of MCP
threat classes. These projects and documents informed which classes are worth
testing. No code was copied from any of them.

  OWASP - MCP Tool Poisoning
    https://owasp.org/www-community/attacks/MCP_Tool_Poisoning
    Threat definitions for poisoned tool descriptions and tool shadowing.

  Snyk agent-scan (Apache-2.0)
    https://github.com/snyk/agent-scan
    Static scanner for MCP servers and agent skills. Scans declarations before
    use; this project enforces at call time. Read for its risk categories.

  ColPali, tau2-bench and other repositories reviewed during selection are
  recorded in docs/learning/02_foundations.md. None contributed code here.

